Describe the shape suggested by each box plot. Give a reason.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[thick] (0.5,3)--(1.5,3) (3.5,3)--(6.5,3);
\draw[thick] (0.5,2.8)--(0.5,3.2) (6.5,2.8)--(6.5,3.2);
\draw[thick] (1.5,2.6) rectangle (3.5,3.4);
\draw[thick] (2,2.6)--(2,3.4);
\path (-0.1,3) node[left] {$A$};
\draw[thick] (0.5,1.8)--(3.5,1.8) (5.5,1.8)--(6.5,1.8);
\draw[thick] (0.5,1.6)--(0.5,2) (6.5,1.6)--(6.5,2);
\draw[thick] (3.5,1.4) rectangle (5.5,2.2);
\draw[thick] (5,1.4)--(5,2.2);
\path (-0.1,1.8) node[left] {$B$};
\draw[thick] (0.5,0.6)--(2,0.6) (5,0.6)--(6.5,0.6);
\draw[thick] (0.5,0.4)--(0.5,0.8) (6.5,0.4)--(6.5,0.8);
\draw[thick] (2,0.2) rectangle (5,1);
\draw[thick] (3.5,0.2)--(3.5,1);
\path (-0.1,0.6) node[left] {$C$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The box plot shows journey times in minutes. Its five-number summary is $8,20,24,40,52$. Describe the shape suggested by the plot and explain why equal whiskers do not settle the answer.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.12cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(57,0);
\foreach \v in {0,10,20,30,40,50} {\draw (\v,-0.08)--(\v,0.08);\path (\v,-0.12) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[thick] (8,1)--(20,1) (40,1)--(52,1);
\draw[thick] (8,0.8)--(8,1.2) (52,0.8)--(52,1.2);
\draw[thick] (20,0.6) rectangle (40,1.4);
\draw[thick] (24,0.6)--(24,1.4);
\path (28,-0.6) node[below] {Journey time (min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The histogram shows $19$ journey times. Each bin includes its lower boundary and excludes its upper boundary. Which proposed box plot could represent the same data? Check the values as well as the shape.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.13cm,y=0.35cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (7,0)--(59,0);
\draw[->] (7,0)--(7,7);
\foreach \v in {7,17,27,37,47,57} {\draw (\v,0)--(\v,-0.2);\path (\v,-0.25) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \f in {2,4,6} {\path (7,\f) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\f$};}
\draw (7,0) rectangle (17,6);
\draw (17,0) rectangle (27,6);
\draw (27,0) rectangle (37,4);
\draw (37,0) rectangle (47,2);
\draw (47,0) rectangle (57,1);
\path (0,3.5) node[rotate=90] {Frequency};
\path (32,-1.8) node[below] {Journey time (min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.12cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(57,0);
\foreach \v in {0,10,20,30,40,50} {\draw (\v,-0.08)--(\v,0.08);\path (\v,-0.12) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[thick] (8,2.2)--(12,2.2) (30,2.2)--(48,2.2);
\draw[thick] (8,2)--(8,2.4) (48,2)--(48,2.4);
\draw[thick] (12,1.8) rectangle (30,2.6);
\draw[thick] (21,1.8)--(21,2.6);
\path (-2,2.2) node[left] {$A$};
\draw[thick] (8,1)--(30,1) (44,1)--(48,1);
\draw[thick] (8,0.8)--(8,1.2) (48,0.8)--(48,1.2);
\draw[thick] (30,0.6) rectangle (44,1.4);
\draw[thick] (38,0.6)--(38,1.4);
\path (-2,1) node[left] {$B$};
\path (28,-0.6) node[below] {Journey time (min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which proposed box plot represents the dot plot? Explain using its five-number summary and shape.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.55cm,y=0.5cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (1,0)--(11,0);
\foreach \v in {2,...,10} {\draw (\v,-0.12)--(\v,0.12);\path (\v,-0.2) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \x/\n in {2/2,3/2,4/3,5/1,6/2,8/1,10/1} {\foreach \j in {1,...,\n} {\fill (\x,{0.5*\j}) circle (2pt);}}
\path (6,-1.2) node[below] {Journey time (min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.55cm,y=1cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->] (1,0)--(11,0);
\foreach \v in {2,...,10} {\draw (\v,-0.08)--(\v,0.08);\path (\v,-0.12) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[thick] (2,2.2)--(3,2.2) (6,2.2)--(10,2.2);
\draw[thick] (2,2)--(2,2.4) (10,2)--(10,2.4);
\draw[thick] (3,1.8) rectangle (6,2.6);
\draw[thick] (4,1.8)--(4,2.6);
\path (0.5,2.2) node[left] {$A$};
\draw[thick] (2,1)--(6,1) (9,1)--(10,1);
\draw[thick] (2,0.8)--(2,1.2) (10,0.8)--(10,1.2);
\draw[thick] (6,0.6) rectangle (9,1.4);
\draw[thick] (8,0.6)--(8,1.4);
\path (0.5,1) node[left] {$B$};
\path (6,-0.6) node[below] {Journey time (min)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
